# Detached walks of a value in the engine's run-time packages (see
# walks_guard_test.go and docs/adr/0018-value-walks-bounded-by-the-call.md).
#
# A walk (String of an array, JSON, stringValue, a deep or relational
# comparison) made without the call's jsval.Walker is bounded only by fixed
# caps. Each function below makes the number of such walks given, and the
# reason says why the value cannot be one a run built:
#   spec:      a literal of the specification read at parse time: a tree as
#              large as the specification, which its parse already bounds;
#   primitive: a value that is never an array there, whose String is no walk;
#   fallback / trusted input / no walk: as stated.
# function<TAB>count<TAB># reason
internal/expr.(*Scope).getIndex	1	# primitive: null or undefined, named in the TypeError
internal/expr.(*Scope).getProp	1	# primitive: null or undefined, named in the TypeError
internal/expr.(*Scope).indexOfStrict	1	# primitive: null or undefined, named in the TypeError
internal/expr.(*Scope).strDepth	1	# primitive: the String of a value that is not an array (arrays are built with the evaluator's own bounded builder above)
internal/expr.(*compiler).object	2	# primitive: an object literal's key, an expression literal (string, number, boolean, null, regexp)
internal/expr.(*parser).parseObject	1	# primitive: an object literal's key, an expression literal
internal/expr.init	1	# primitive: null or undefined, named in the TypeError
internal/expr.indataVisitor	1	# primitive: an expression literal argument (indata's field), named in the error
internal/expr.literalArg	1	# primitive: an expression literal argument
internal/expr.scaleVisitor	1	# primitive: an expression literal argument
internal/expr.selectionTuples	1	# primitive: an index number
internal/format.NumberLocaleFromValue	4	# spec: config.locale.number, read once as the view is made
internal/scale.init	1	# no walk: the built-in palettes are colour strings, shared by every call
internal/scene.(*Item).Walker	1	# fallback: an item outside a scene (the package's tests); every mark vega makes carries the call's Walker (Scenegraph.SetWalker)
internal/scene.FromJSON	1	# trusted input: serialized scenes the tests and fuzz targets load; no public API or render path calls it
internal/transforms/contour.KDE2D	1	# fallback: no key function given (the package's tests); vega passes the call's transforms.KeyStringer
internal/transforms/hierarchy.Nest	1	# fallback: no key function given (the package's tests); vega passes the call's transforms.KeyStringer
internal/transforms/hierarchy.Stratify	1	# fallback: no key function given (the package's tests); vega passes the call's transforms.KeyStringer
internal/transforms/wordcloud.Transform	1	# fallback: no text function given (the package's tests); vega passes the call's transforms.KeyStringer
internal/vega.(*Scope).compareRef	2	# spec: a literal of the specification, read as the view is parsed (tree-shaped, as large as the specification)
internal/vega.(*Scope).fieldRef	1	# spec: a literal of the specification, read as the view is parsed (tree-shaped, as large as the specification)
internal/vega.(*Scope).keyRef	1	# spec: a literal of the specification, read as the view is parsed (tree-shaped, as large as the specification)
